5. Use `/pastdev-memory` with your app request.

```text
/pastdev-memory Add a private project notebook with past.dev. Store dated notes and answer questions with source excerpts. Test access with two users.
```

[Lovable skills](https://docs.lovable.dev/features/skills) can also apply when a request matches their description. The connector supplies API access. The skill supplies the implementation and test procedure.

> **Scope**
>
> Neither the connector nor the skill installs event hooks. They do not automatically capture Lovable conversations or recall memory before every prompt.

## Build a memory example

Link the connection to your project. Start with an app that stores project notes and answers questions with dated sources. Use this prompt after the connection passes its test.

```text
Build a project notebook with the past.dev connector. Require sign-in.
Derive the user's identity on the server.
Create a separate fixed audience for each user.
Store each note with a stable source id, its event time, and that audience.
Keep identity and audience outside all model-controlled inputs.
Show a pending state until the ingestion status is completed.
Recall notes as the authenticated user.
Show each answer with source excerpts and dates.
State when the evidence does not support an answer.
Keep credentials in the connector.
Test two users, a changed deadline, and a question with no supporting source.
```

> **Access**
>
> A shared API connection does not authenticate your app's users. Server code must check each user and select their identity and audience. An ingest identity identifies the author only. A source without an audience is visible to the whole project.

## Verify the result

1. Connect with a valid project key and confirm that the credential test succeeds.
2. Confirm that an invalid key fails the credential test.
3. Store a note for user A in user A's audience.
4. Wait until the send reports `completed`.
5. Recall as user A and check the source id and excerpt.
6. Recall as user B and confirm that user A's private source is absent.
7. Add a later note with a changed deadline and a new source id.
8. Check the current answer and its dated evidence.
9. Ask a question that the stored notes cannot answer.
10. Confirm that the app states the evidence limit.

Check the [setup guide](/docs/memory-api/setup) for audience creation and completion checks. Check [access control](/docs/memory-api/access-control) before you add shared data. The [benchmarks](/benchmarks) describe recall measurement; they do not replace tests of your app.

